# xenclient-oe (OpenXT layer-split monorepo)

OpenEmbedded / Yocto layers for OpenXT, split into base, domains, and UI
layers, with hierarchical **kas** configuration for product image builds.

## Repository layout

| Path                   | Description                                              |
| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `meta-openxt-base/`    | Foundation recipes (dom0, installer, stubdomain, shared) |
| `meta-openxt-domains/` | Service domain images (NDVM, USBVM, SyncVM, …)           |
| `meta-openxt-ui/`      | UI stack (UIVM, vglass-facing product pieces)            |
| `kas/`                 | Hierarchical kas configs and compositions                |
| `scripts/`             | Host setup, kas workspace init, deploy/ISO helpers       |
| `docs/`                | Implementation plans and design notes                    |
| `LAYERS.md`            | Layer ownership and bblayers guidance                    |

## Quick start (kas)

```bash
# From the monorepo root
./scripts/setup-host.sh

# Create / select a workspace and build instance (OE-style init)
source ./scripts/kas-init-build-env [WORKSPACE] [INSTANCE]

# Checkout layers (first time) and build
kas checkout kas/dom0.yml
kas build kas/dom0.yml

# Or drive several images through the helper
./scripts/kas-build-all.sh initramfs stubdomain dom0
```

After init, use ordinary kas entry points — no config-prefix helper is
required. See **`kas/README.md`** for the full workspace model.

### Important environment

| Variable                | Meaning                                      | Default                                  |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `OPENXT_KAS_WORKSPACE`  | Workspace root (layers + caches + instances) | `<parent>/openxt-kas`                    |
| `OPENXT_KAS_INSTANCE`   | Build instance name                          | `default`                                |
| `KAS_BUILD_DIR`         | Per-instance kas/bitbake directory           | `$WORKSPACE/build-$INSTANCE`             |
| `DL_DIR` / `SSTATE_DIR` | Shared download and sstate caches            | `$WORKSPACE/downloads`, `…/sstate-cache` |
| `OPENXT_CERTS_DIR`      | Signing certificates                         | `$WORKSPACE/certs`                       |
| `OPENXT_LAYER_IMPORT`   | Optional explicit layer import directory     | unset                                    |
| `OPENXT_PYTHON3`        | CPython 3.11 for Dunfell bitbake             | auto-detect `python3.11`                 |

### Product entry points

| Entry                | Composition            | Typical target                       |
| -------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `kas/initramfs.yml`  | headless / base        | xenclient-initramfs-image            |
| `kas/stubdomain.yml` | headless / base        | xenclient-stubdomain-initramfs-image |
| `kas/dom0.yml`       | headless / base        | xenclient-dom0-image                 |
| `kas/installer.yml`  | headless / base        | xenclient-installer-image            |
| `kas/ndvm.yml`       | domains                | xenclient-ndvm-image                 |
| `kas/usbvm.yml`      | domains                | usbvm-image                          |
| `kas/syncvm.yml`     | domains                | xenclient-syncvm-image               |
| `kas/uivm.yml`       | full (base+domains+ui) | xenclient-uivm-image                 |

Recommended order: **initramfs** and **stubdomain** before **dom0** (dom0
packages stubdomain artefacts).

## Workspace layout (after init)

```text
$OPENXT_KAS_WORKSPACE/     # default: <parent-of-monorepo>/openxt-kas
  layers/                  # OE + platform checkouts
  downloads/               # shared DL_DIR
  sstate-cache/            # shared SSTATE_DIR
  certs/                   # shared signing material
  build-<instance>/        # KAS_BUILD_DIR (conf/, tmp/, deploy)

$OPENXT_ROOT/layers  ->  $WORKSPACE/layers   # gitignored symlink
```

Committed kas YAML uses `path: layers/<repo>` relative to this monorepo.
Shared caches use `${TOPDIR}/../…` next to each instance build directory.

Optional one-time import of existing clones (explicit only; nothing is
auto-detected):

```bash
OPENXT_LAYER_IMPORT=/path/to/layers \
  source ./scripts/kas-init-build-env /data/openxt-kas default
```

## Installer ISO (post-process)

```bash
export OPENXT_CERTS_DIR="${OPENXT_KAS_WORKSPACE}/certs"
./scripts/stage-repository.sh
./scripts/deploy-iso.sh
# -> $KAS_BUILD_DIR/staging/iso/
```

